return PlaceObj('ModDef', {
	'title', "Super Big Map",
	'description', "Super Big Map\n\n3x more map. No extra fries.\n\nOn the Colony Site screen, toggle EXPAND MAP before pressing START. Expanded new games use a 20 x 20 sector grid, giving you 300 additional sectors to explore and build on. The native vanilla terrain is generated once and proportionally stretched across the expanded destination; no terrain mirroring or alternate expansion mode is used. Leave EXPAND MAP off for a completely vanilla game: all Super Big Map gameplay, UI, camera, and generation changes remain disabled.\n\nExpanded-map zoom can be changed in Game Options -> Options -> Display -> Max Zoom Level.\n\nRequirements and Compatibility:\n\nYou must start a new game with EXPAND MAP enabled. Existing saves will not be expanded.\nInitial loading takes longer because the expanded map requires more processing.\nDo not use other zoom mods. SBM includes its own zoom settings for expanded maps.\n\n[IMPORTANT]: Quit and restart the game after enabling this mod to clear cached data.\nTested on Surviving Mars Relaunched v1.1.1.405907 on Windows 11. This compatibility version is Lua-only and needs no executable patch. Start a new expanded game; pre-update expanded saves have not been validated.\n\nFeedback and bug reports: https://smr-mods-feedback.fredware.app or https://github.com/facazevedo/surviving-mars-relaunched-mods/issues",
	'short_description', "Adds an opt-in stretch-generated 20 x 20 map expansion.",
	'image', "Mod/SuperBigMap/Images/final_composed.jpg",
	'last_changes', "Rock clearance checks skip clipping terrain cells proven outside the mesh face, retaining exact results. Expanded anomaly targets now preserve the native generator's requested counts even when its placement grid is crowded. Decoration contact bounds are refreshed when a captured rotation changes. Exact terrain-cell planes are reused within each decoration clearance check to reduce loading work. Floating-rock proposal checks stop once actual terrain contact disproves a floating mesh; complete clearance and placement proofs are retained. Fixed surface loading failures when one rock detail level touches another decoration while other detail levels float; safely seats the rock without removing decorations or adding a whole-map scan. Integrated compatibility for Mars Expedition Deluxe v55 elevator and terminal map queries, Omega Telescope v37 load counters, and the debug Load screen mod-list preview. Resource landing areas now account for the game's connected buildable-area and height-spread limits on sloped terrain. Crowded-map anomaly placement avoids repeatedly searching exhausted candidates and skips areas already ruled out by deposit spacing. Residual anomaly placement now searches remaining legal hexes when random candidates are exhausted. Native underground deposits are relocated before new deposits reserve the available space. Native rock corrections refused by unknown neighbouring geometry now use the existing keep-in-place policy. Fixed grey overviews and unavailable outer-sector scanning after an interrupted expansion. Crowded maps with extra anomalies renew their placement search budget for each missing anomaly. Existing saves with this specific late density failure recover their entrances without regenerating the colony; valid completed elevators stay in place. Second Colony entrances no longer block the main map entrance check. Starting breakthrough rewards wait for final terrain, fixing new-game failures with Start with all Breakthroughs. Fixed Astrogeologist's starting Rare Metals deposit and Hydro Engineer's starting Water deposit being hidden by expanded-map scanning. Existing expanded saves repair a missing commander deposit on load. All 18 commander profiles checked, including save/reload. Smoother map edges: the straight seams in the vanilla border terrain are now repaired without leaving walls, trenches or streaks where a repaired seam fades out. Unexplored underground areas are completely dark on PC, and an underground sector's buildable area reads \"?\" in every language until about half of the sector has been surveyed. Fixed a save error after placing an Elevator, the surface brightening for a moment after leaving the underground, and a \"mod-related problem\" warning when starting some sites. Rare startup failures from decorative rocks losing their original terrain clearance or being seated against the wrong terrain sample are fixed. New maps no longer stop with a resource cluster error such as \"extractors=1/2\": a cluster that cannot get its planned extractors now uses higher-grade deposits or keeps fewer resources. Works with More Deposits: deposits whose grade that mod fixes are no longer counted as premium, so resource clusters keep their normal composition. A cluster landing pad beside a steep slope is now levelled wide enough to stay buildable. Very crowded maps no longer fail because a few anomalies could not be placed. Two neighbouring resource clusters no longer receive an anomaly or dome bonus meant for the other. Rock pieces left floating by the map stretch (a few centimetres above a steep slope, or stones leaning only on each other) are now seated instead of stopping map generation. Vanilla rocks are no longer relocated far from their original spot: one that cannot be seated nearby keeps its place. Fixed long stutters in large late-game colonies when a waste rock site has no reachable dump spot. On the Colony Site screen the ribbon behind THREATS and RESOURCES now ends at the longest name, and EXPAND MAP no longer widens the title strip. In the overview, pointing outside the map (surface or underground) no longer highlights or queues an edge sector. Fixed stutters and multi-second freezes in large colonies with many drones or automated RC Terraformers (drone task swaps, landscaping approaches and unreachable sites no longer run hundreds of path searches). Fixed an error logged when the overview opens before the camera is ready. Works with ProductionOverUnder in debug builds: its infobar arrows no longer raise localization asserts. Smoother at high game speeds in large colonies: drone task swaps no longer run path searches, and heat lookups are cheaper. Colonist walking-distance checks search only the area a walkable path can use, and RC Terraformers pick the nearest waste rock pile without path searches. Automated Explorers no longer re-search anomalies they cannot reach every hour; they check again as soon as nearby terrain, tunnels or landscaping change. Tested on v1.1.1.405907.",
